# `.claude/rules/`

Topic-scoped rules. Each file is a markdown doc with optional YAML frontmatter.

## Why this directory exists

Root `CLAUDE.md` is loaded once at session start and cached in memory — mid-session edits don't apply until `/compact` or restart. Path-scoped rules in this directory load **on demand** when Claude reads a matching file, so edits take effect on the next matching read.

Use this directory once `CLAUDE.md` exceeds ~200 lines, or when a rule only applies to a specific file type / sub-area.

## File layout

```
.claude/rules/
├── README.md           # this file (advisory; loads at session start because it has no paths:)
├── testing.md          # scoped to test files
├── api.md              # scoped to API code
└── frontend/
    └── react.md        # nested layout works too — discovered recursively
```

## Format

Always-on rule (loads at session start, like CLAUDE.md):

```markdown
# Testing conventions

- Always run `pnpm test` before claiming work done.
- Test files live next to source: `foo.ts` → `foo.test.ts`.
```

Path-scoped rule — only loads when Claude reads a matching file:

```markdown
---
paths:
  - "**/*.test.ts"
  - "**/*.test.tsx"
---

# Test file conventions

- Mock external dependencies, not internal modules.
- One behaviour per test.
- Clean up side effects in `afterEach`.
```

## Caveats

- Path-scoped rules trigger when matching files are **read**, not on every tool use. Bash-generated edits or `Write` to new files won't trigger them — keep must-follow rules unscoped (in root `CLAUDE.md` or unscoped here).
- After `/compact`, path-scoped rules are dropped from history until another matching file is read.
- Globs use `.gitignore`-style patterns. Test with `git ls-files` to confirm matches.

## Linting

`/mastersoft:verify` (Sonnet-backed) checks rule glob coverage, broken refs, and contradictions with the actual codebase. Triggered when load-brief flags issues.
